# userspace-dp/MIRI.registry -- the modules `make test-miri` actually runs
# under Miri (#9499 member 2).
#
# FORMAT: <module-path>  <min-passed>  <one-line reason>
#
#   module-path   the `cargo miri test` filter, e.g. `afxdp::types::cos::`.
#                 It must resolve to a real file under userspace-dp/src/;
#                 scripts/miri-census.sh FAILS if it does not, because a
#                 registry entry pointing at a module that no longer exists is
#                 the silent-shrink failure wearing a green face.
#   min-passed    the floor `make test-miri` asserts against the module's
#                 `test result: ok. N passed` line. A MISSING result line and
#                 `0 passed` are both FAILURES, never skips -- a leg that ran
#                 nothing and exited 0 is exactly what this registry exists to
#                 make impossible.
#   reason        why this module is worth the Miri budget, in one line.
#
# WHY A REGISTRY AND NOT `miri test` OVER THE CRATE
#
#   Measured at 16df7c8c7: `cargo +nightly miri test --bins -- afxdp::frame::`
#   ran 1021 s and then stopped on an `unsupported operation: open ... when
#   isolation is enabled` from a test that reads a file. Miri over this crate
#   is neither fast nor uniformly clean, so the honest shape is a named subset
#   plus a census that makes every module OUTSIDE the subset say so in writing
#   (userspace-dp/MIRI.unregistered).
#
# HOW THIS SHRINKS SAFELY
#
#   It cannot shrink silently. Deleting a line here does not make the leg
#   quieter -- it makes scripts/miri-census.sh report every miri-coverage claim
#   that line was covering as undeclared, and the census exits 1. Removing a
#   module for real is therefore a two-part edit that names its own reason in
#   MIRI.unregistered, which is the visible-cost property #9499 asks for.
#
afxdp::types::cos::  12  FlowFairState::new_boxed writes MaybeUninit fields through raw pointers; Miri is the only oracle in the tree that can see a missed field or a bad drop target. Measured clean at 16df7c8c7: 12 passed, 76 s, no unsupported operations.
